IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Article 4, security of processing.
-- LAYER 1. A rule named "... the provider must ..." says whether the duty binds on the stated facts; a rule named
-- "... the provider's duty ... is met" says whether it was met once it binds. JUST TRUE = the text says yes, JUST FALSE = the
-- text says no in its own words, NOTHING = not covered (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- Art 4(5) (the Commission's power to adopt technical implementing measures, and the regulatory procedure with scrutiny) is
-- machinery and is inert (reason 2) in NOTES.md.

§ `Article 4 -- security of processing`

§§ `Art 4(1) -- appropriate technical and organisational measures`

-- src:52 | The provider of a publicly available electronic communications service must take appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard security of its services, if necessary in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network with respect to network security.
@ref Art 4(1) first sentence (src:52) row:A4(1).s1
GIVEN `the provider has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the security of its services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `acting in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network is necessary with respect to network security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has acted in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) first sentence the provider's duty to take appropriate measures is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must take appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard security of its services" -- FORK F8: "appropriate" is the person's plain input
        IF NOT `the provider has taken appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the security of its services` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if necessary in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network with respect to network security" -- FORK F7: a bare "must" whose "if necessary" limb is not done
        IF `acting in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network is necessary with respect to network security` AND (NOT `the provider has acted in conjunction with the provider of the public communications network`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:52 | Having regard to the state of the art and the cost of their implementation, these measures shall ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented.
@ref Art 4(1) second sentence (src:52) row:A4(1).s2
GIVEN `the measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost of their implementation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) second sentence the measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk` MEANS
    IF `the measures ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented, having regard to the state of the art and the cost of their implementation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "these measures shall ensure a level of security appropriate to the risk presented" -- FORK F8: "appropriate to the risk" is the person's plain input
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 4(1a) -- the minimum content of the measures, and audit`

-- src:54 | Without prejudice to Directive 95/46/EC, the measures referred to in paragraph 1 shall at least:
-- src:55 | ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes,
-- src:56 | protect personal data stored or transmitted against accidental or unlawful destruction, accidental loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure, and,
-- src:57 | ensure the implementation of a security policy with respect to the processing of personal data,
@ref Art 4(1a) chapeau and the three dashes (src:54-57) row:A4(1a).chapeau row:A4(1a).dash1 row:A4(1a).dash2 row:A4(1a).dash3
GIVEN `the measures ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures protect personal data stored or transmitted against accidental or unlawful destruction, accidental loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures ensure the implementation of a security policy with respect to the processing of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1a) the measures include at least what the three dashes require` MEANS
    IF `the measures ensure that personal data can be accessed only by authorised personnel for legally authorised purposes`
       AND `the measures protect personal data stored or transmitted against accidental or unlawful destruction, accidental loss or alteration, and unauthorised or unlawful storage, processing, access or disclosure`
       AND `the measures ensure the implementation of a security policy with respect to the processing of personal data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the measures referred to in paragraph 1 shall at least"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:58 | Relevant national authorities shall be able to audit the measures taken by providers of publicly available electronic communication services and to issue recommendations about best practices concerning the level of security which those measures should achieve.
@ref Art 4(1a) closing sentence (src:58) row:A4(1a).audit
GIVEN `the body is a relevant national authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1a) the national authority can audit the provider's measures and issue recommendations` MEANS
    IF `the body is a relevant national authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names relevant national authorities and is silent on any other body
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Art 4(2) -- a particular risk of a breach of network security`

-- src:60 | In case of a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network, the provider of a publicly available electronic communications service must inform the subscribers concerning such risk
@ref Art 4(2) first limb (src:60) row:A4(2)
GIVEN `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers concerning the risk` MEANS
    IF `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In case of a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network" -- FORK F6: a failed "in case of" read as the text's no
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:60 | and, where the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider, of any possible remedies, including an indication of the likely costs involved.
@ref Art 4(2) second limb (src:60) row:A4(2)
GIVEN `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(2) the provider must inform the subscribers of any possible remedies, including the likely costs` MEANS
    IF `there is a particular risk of a breach of the security of the network` AND `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider" -- a "where" condition that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F6
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- Compliance, once the duty binds (a particular risk exists).
-- src:60 | the provider of a publicly available electronic communications service must inform the subscribers concerning such risk and, where the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider, of any possible remedies, including an indication of the likely costs involved.
@ref Art 4(2) (src:60) row:A4(2)
GIVEN `the provider has informed the subscribers concerning the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has informed the subscribers of any possible remedies, including an indication of the likely costs involved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(2) the provider's duty to inform the subscribers is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must inform the subscribers concerning such risk"
        IF NOT `the provider has informed the subscribers concerning the risk` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "of any possible remedies, including an indication of the likely costs involved"
        IF `the risk lies outside the scope of the measures to be taken by the service provider` AND (NOT `the provider has informed the subscribers of any possible remedies, including an indication of the likely costs involved`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The text fixes no time for it, so the rule has no WITHIN.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 4(2) the provider informs the subscribers of the risk` MEANS
    PARTY `the provider`
    MUST `inform the subscribers of the risk`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the provider` BECAUSE "Art 4(2): the subscribers were not informed of the particular risk of a breach of the security of the network"

§§ `Art 4(3) -- personal data breach`

-- src:62 | In the case of a personal data breach, the provider of publicly available electronic communications services shall, without undue delay, notify the personal data breach to the competent national authority.
@ref Art 4(3) first subparagraph (src:62) row:A4(3).p1
GIVEN `there has been a personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider must notify the competent national authority` MEANS
    IF `there has been a personal data breach`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a personal data breach" -- FORK F6: a failed "in the case of" read as the text's no
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:62 | the provider of publicly available electronic communications services shall, without undue delay, notify the personal data breach to the competent national authority.
@ref Art 4(3) first subparagraph (src:62) row:A4(3).p1
GIVEN `the provider notified the personal data breach to the competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider did so without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider's duty to notify the authority is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider notified the personal data breach to the competent national authority` AND `the provider did so without undue delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, without undue delay, notify the personal data breach to the competent national authority"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. "Without undue delay" is not a number: `the time that counts as undue delay` is the
-- caller's input (in hours), never a figure from the text (FORK F9).
GIVEN `the time that counts as undue delay, in hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 4(3) first subparagraph the provider notifies the authority` MEANS
    PARTY `the provider`
    MUST `notify the authority of the personal data breach`
    WITHIN `the time that counts as undue delay, in hours`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the provider` BECAUSE "Art 4(3) first subparagraph: the personal data breach was not notified to the competent national authority without undue delay"

-- src:63 | When the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual, the provider shall also notify the subscriber or individual of the breach without undue delay.
@ref Art 4(3) second subparagraph (src:63) row:A4(3).p2
GIVEN `there has been a personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider must also notify the subscriber or individual` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a personal data breach" -- FORK F6: a failed "in the case of" read as the text's no
        IF NOT `there has been a personal data breach` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the personal data breach is likely to adversely affect the personal data or privacy of a subscriber or individual" -- a "when" condition that fails (periods ruling (b), (c)); FORK F6
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:63 | the provider shall also notify the subscriber or individual of the breach without undue delay.
@ref Art 4(3) second subparagraph (src:63) row:A4(3).p2
GIVEN `the provider notified the subscriber or individual of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider did so without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider's duty to notify the subscriber or individual is met` MEANS
    IF `the provider notified the subscriber or individual of the breach` AND `the provider did so without undue delay`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the provider shall also notify the subscriber or individual of the breach without undue delay"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

GIVEN `the time that counts as undue delay, in hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 4(3) second subparagraph the provider notifies the subscriber or individual` MEANS
    PARTY `the provider`
    MUST `notify the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach`
    WITHIN `the time that counts as undue delay, in hours`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the provider` BECAUSE "Art 4(3) second subparagraph: the subscriber or individual was not notified of the personal data breach without undue delay"

-- src:64 | Notification of a personal data breach to a subscriber or individual concerned shall not be required if the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures, and that those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach.
-- src:64 | Such technological protection measures shall render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it.
@ref Art 4(3) third subparagraph (src:64) row:A4(3).p3.s1 row:A4(3).p3.s2
GIVEN `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) third subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual is required` MEANS
    IF `the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority that it has implemented appropriate technological protection measures`
       AND `those measures were applied to the data concerned by the security breach`
       AND `those measures render the data unintelligible to any person who is not authorised to access it`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be required if the provider has demonstrated to the satisfaction of the competent authority" -- FORK F8: the authority's satisfaction is the person's plain input
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence says when notification is NOT required; where its conditions are not all met it does not say that it is required (the second subparagraph does)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:65 | Without prejudice to the provider's obligation to notify subscribers and individuals concerned, if the provider has not already notified the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach, the competent national authority, having considered the likely adverse effects of the breach, may require it to do so.
@ref Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph (src:65) row:A4(3).p4
GIVEN `the provider has not already notified the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the competent national authority has considered the likely adverse effects of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) fourth subparagraph the competent national authority may require the provider to notify the subscriber or individual` MEANS
    IF `the provider has not already notified the subscriber or individual of the personal data breach` AND `the competent national authority has considered the likely adverse effects of the breach`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power ("may require") whose "if" gate has failed; the text does not close the gate with "only" (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:66 | The notification to the subscriber or individual shall at least describe the nature of the personal data breach and the contact points where more information can be obtained, and shall recommend measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach.
@ref Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph, first sentence (src:66) row:A4(3).p5.s1
GIVEN `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the subscriber or individual has the content required` MEANS
    IF `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach`
       AND `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained`
       AND `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall at least describe the nature of the personal data breach"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:66 | The notification to the competent national authority shall, in addition, describe the consequences of, and the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address, the personal data breach.
@ref Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph, second sentence (src:66) row:A4(3).p5.s2
GIVEN `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification describes the consequences of the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification describes the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address the personal data breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(3) fifth subparagraph the notification to the competent national authority has the content required` MEANS
    -- "in addition" is read as cumulative: everything the first sentence requires, and the consequences and measures (FORK F10)
    IF `the notification describes the nature of the personal data breach`
       AND `the notification describes the contact points where more information can be obtained`
       AND `the notification recommends measures to mitigate the possible adverse effects of the personal data breach`
       AND `the notification describes the consequences of the personal data breach`
       AND `the notification describes the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address the personal data breach`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, in addition, describe the consequences of, and the measures proposed or taken by the provider to address, the personal data breach" -- FORK F10: "in addition" read as cumulative
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `Art 4(4) -- guidelines, audit, sanctions and the inventory`

-- src:67 | Subject to any technical implementing measures adopted under paragraph 5, the competent national authorities may adopt guidelines and, where necessary, issue instructions concerning the circumstances in which providers are required to notify personal data breaches, the format of such notification and the manner in which the notification is to be made.
@ref Art 4(4) first subparagraph, first sentence (src:67) row:A4(4).p1.s1
GIVEN `the measure concerns the circumstances in which providers are required to notify personal data breaches, the format of the notification or the manner in which it is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is an instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instruction is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `technical implementing measures adopted under paragraph 5 cover the point` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority may adopt the guideline or issue the instruction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any technical implementing measures adopted under paragraph 5" -- their content is not in the sources
        IF `technical implementing measures adopted under paragraph 5 cover the point` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is stated for the circumstances, format and manner of notification only
        IF NOT `the measure concerns the circumstances in which providers are required to notify personal data breaches, the format of the notification or the manner in which it is made` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where necessary, issue instructions" -- a "where" gate on a power that fails (periods ruling (b)); FORK F11 (grant and power ruling item 3: listed, not changed)
        IF `the measure is an instruction` AND (NOT `the instruction is necessary`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:67 | They shall also be able to audit whether providers have complied with their notification obligations under this paragraph, and shall impose appropriate sanctions in the event of a failure to do so.
@ref Art 4(4) first subparagraph, second sentence (src:67) row:A4(4).p1.s2
GIVEN `the body is a competent national authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority can audit the provider's compliance with its notification obligations` MEANS
    IF `the body is a competent national authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names the competent national authorities
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:67 | and shall impose appropriate sanctions in the event of a failure to do so.
@ref Art 4(4) first subparagraph, second sentence (src:67) row:A4(4).p1.s2
GIVEN `the provider has failed to comply with its notification obligations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(4) first subparagraph the competent national authority must impose appropriate sanctions on the provider` MEANS
    IF `the provider has failed to comply with its notification obligations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the event of a failure to do so" -- FORK F6: a failed "in the event of" read as the text's no
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:68 | Providers shall maintain an inventory of personal data breaches comprising the facts surrounding the breach, its effects and the remedial action taken which shall be sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with the provisions of paragraph 3.
-- src:68 | The inventory shall only include the information necessary for this purpose.
@ref Art 4(4) second subparagraph (src:68) row:A4(4).p2.s1 row:A4(4).p2.s2
GIVEN `the inventory comprises the facts surrounding the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inventory comprises the effects of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inventory comprises the remedial action taken` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inventory is sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the inventory includes only the information necessary for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(4) second subparagraph the provider's inventory of personal data breaches is as required` MEANS
    IF `the inventory comprises the facts surrounding the breach`
       AND `the inventory comprises the effects of the breach`
       AND `the inventory comprises the remedial action taken`
       AND `the inventory is sufficient to enable the competent national authorities to verify compliance with paragraph 3`
       AND `the inventory includes only the information necessary for this purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The inventory shall only include the information necessary for this purpose"
    ELSE JUST FALSE
